{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '895,945p;2150,2245p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '375,455p;525,575p'\"","aggregated_output":"   895\t   is served and dialed over, and `:write-heads!` the file replace\n   896\t   `heads.edn` is written with (yin.repl.dht/open).  A `(require ...)` of\n   897\t   a name that is absent while a followed principal has no installed\n   898\t   head stays pending until that head is installed.\n   899\t\n   900\t   `:custody` is an optional custody composition value\n   901\t   (yin.vm.ucf.compose): the shell only carries it, as data, so the\n   902\t   host's single step owner can advance it (yin.repl.main/step-all --\n   903\t   the custody control step runs during hydration and through the\n   904\t   bounded shutdown drain; the custody program step runs only while\n   905\t   the shell is admitted and running).  Nothing in the shell reads or\n   906\t   steps it; nil, the default, is today's behaviour.\n   907\t\n   908\t   `:frontends` is the frontend catalog (`yang.frontend`) the session\n   909\t   compiles through, composed by the host entry point (this namespace\n   910\t   requires no frontend; see `yin.repl.frontends`).  Without it the catalog\n   911\t   is empty and every compile answers `unavailable-parser`.  The session\n   912\t   pins this immutable snapshot: installing into another catalog value\n   913\t   never changes a live session.  `:lang` selects a frontend by id\n   914\t   (`:yang/python`) or by `[id revision]`; a language keyword is not a\n   915\t   selector. The default is the `:yang/clojure` frontend.\n   916\t   one the catalog cannot answer is an `unavailable-parser` diagnostic,\n   917\t   never a fallback to another frontend.\"\n   918\t  ([] (create-state {}))\n   919\t  ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n   920\t            content-store content-client name-env link-policy index-store\n   921\t            index-store-spec dht-key principals ws-host write-heads! custody\n   922\t            frontends admission]\n   923\t     :or {lang :yang/clojure vm-type :semantic admission {}}}]\n   924\t   (let [output-stream (or output-stream (make-output-medium!))\n   925\t         output-cursor (or output-cursor (mint-cursor output-stream))\n   926\t         shell-token (str (random-uuid))\n   927\t         index-store-spec (cond\n   928\t                            (and index-store index-store-spec)\n   929\t                            (throw (ex-info\n   930\t                                     (str \"yin.repl/create-state takes one \"\n   931\t                                          \"index store: :index-store-spec \"\n   932\t                                          \"(mem or a file directory) or \"\n   933\t                                          \":index-store (a dao.jing handle), \"\n   934\t                                          \"not both\")\n   935\t                                     {:index-store-spec index-store-spec}))\n   936\t\n   937\t                            index-store nil\n   938\t\n   939\t                            :else (store/checked-spec index-store-spec))\n   940\t         ;; composed before the store opens: a refused composition never\n   941\t         ;; holds a directory lock\n   942\t         link-source (link/composition\n   943\t                       {:name-env name-env\n   944\t                        :content-store content-store\n   945\t                        :content-client content-client\n  2150\t        (= :incomplete (probe combined))\n  2151\t        (pos? (bracket-balance combined)))\n  2152\t      [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n  2153\t\n  2154\t      :else\n  2155\t      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n  2156\t            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n  2157\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  2158\t                                  :clj Exception\n  2159\t                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n  2160\t                          {:error error}))]\n  2161\t        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n  2162\t\n  2163\t\n  2164\t(defn repl-state\n  2165\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n  2166\t\n  2167\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n  2168\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n  2169\t   operation.\n  2170\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n  2171\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n  2172\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n  2173\t   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n  2174\t   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n  2175\t   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n  2176\t   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n  2177\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n  2178\t   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n  2179\t   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n  2180\t   `:index-publication` exposes the verified code-log cursor and covered\n  2181\t   transaction count for owner diagnostics, never a substitute query view.\n  2182\t   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n  2183\t   of its `$ast` and `$occ` relations, whether a gap lost it, and why it\n  2184\t   failed.\"\n  2185\t  [state]\n  2186\t  {:lang (:lang state)\n  2187\t   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n  2188\t                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n  2189\t                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n  2190\t                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n  2191\t   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n  2192\t        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n  2193\t        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n  2194\t        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n  2195\t                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n  2196\t                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n  2197\t   :running? (:running? state)\n  2198\t   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n  2199\t            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n  2200\t   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  2201\t              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n  2202\t                (mapv (fn [p]\n  2203\t                        {:name (:name p)\n  2204\t                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n  2205\t                         :policy (if (fn? policy) :fn policy)\n  2206\t                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n  2207\t                      (:links parked))))\n  2208\t   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n  2209\t   :index-publication (select-keys (get-in state [:indexer :materialization])\n  2210\t                                   [:cursor :transactions :manifest-address])\n  2211\t   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n  2212\t   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n  2213\t   :remote {:connected? false}})\n   375\t                                      {:content-store (:content-store ix)\n   376\t                                       :intake intake :mode :resolved :schema {}})\n   377\t              expected (- (:transactions ix) transactions)]\n   378\t          (loop [cursor cursor, consumer consumer, n 0]\n   379\t            (let [r (stream/next (:local ix) cursor)]\n   380\t              (when (stream/valid-outcome? :next r)\n   381\t                (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   382\t                  :dao.stream/ok\n   383\t                  (when (< n expected)\n   384\t                    (let [consumer' (index/fold-batch consumer (:dao.stream/value r))]\n   385\t                      (when (zero? (:rejected consumer'))\n   386\t                        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) consumer' (inc n)))))\n   387\t                  (:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end)\n   388\t                  (when (= n expected) {:cursor cursor :consumer consumer})\n   389\t                  nil)))))\n   390\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   391\t          nil)))))\n   392\t\n   393\t\n   394\t(defn- enqueue-publication\n   395\t  \"Full reconstruction when no validated frontier is available; otherwise\n   396\t   publication of the suffix-folded trees through the existing indexer.\"\n   397\t  [ix]\n   398\t  (let [{:keys [transactor intake]} (:publication ix)]\n   399\t    (if-let [{:keys [cursor consumer]} (suffix-state ix intake)]\n   400\t      (let [;; A fresh round has exactly one intake; still honor the\n   401\t            ;; caller's selection function and its pool-membership rule.\n   402\t            select-stream (:select-stream (:publish-opts ix) first)\n   403\t            selected (when (fn? select-stream) (select-stream [intake]))\n   404\t            _ (when-not (identical? selected intake)\n   405\t                (throw (ex-info \"publication must select its round's intake\" {})))\n   406\t            {:keys [status state]} (index/publish! consumer)\n   407\t            manifest (get-in state [:publish :manifest])]\n   408\t        (when-not (= :ok status)\n   409\t          (throw (ex-info \"complete-retention publication intake refused\" {:status status})))\n   410\t        {:cursor cursor :manifest manifest :manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest)})\n   411\t      (let [result (transactor/publish! transactor (:publish-opts ix))\n   412\t            tail (stream/cursor (:local ix) :dao.stream/newest)]\n   413\t        (when-not (and (stream/valid-outcome? :cursor tail)\n   414\t                       (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome tail)))\n   415\t          (throw (ex-info \"published log frontier could not be read\" {:result tail})))\n   416\t        (assoc result :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor tail))))))\n   417\t\n   418\t\n   419\t(defn- publish\n   420\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction, using\n   421\t   the retained frontier when valid, drain the intake, and read the\n   422\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   423\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   424\t   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   425\t   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   426\t   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   427\t   unpublished.\"\n   428\t  [ix round]\n   429\t  (try\n   430\t    (let [{:keys [pool]} (:publication ix)\n   431\t          {:keys [manifest-address manifest cursor]} (enqueue-publication ix)\n   432\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   433\t      (if defect\n   434\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   435\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   436\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   437\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   438\t            (cond-> (assoc ix\n   439\t                           :manifest-address manifest-address\n   440\t                           :published (:transactions ix)\n   441\t                           :published-payloads n\n   442\t                           :materialization {:cursor cursor\n   443\t                                             :transactions (:transactions ix)\n   444\t                                             :manifest-address manifest-address\n   445\t                                             :manifest manifest\n   446\t                                             :max-t (dec (transactor/watermark (:allocator ix)))})\n   447\t              (= :publish (:stage (:failure ix))) (assoc :failure nil)))))\n   448\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   449\t      (assoc ix\n   450\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t(defn- consume\n   454\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   455\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   525\t            :publication)))\n   526\t\n   527\t\n   528\t(defn skip\n   529\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium without\n   530\t   indexing it: a round that threw before its program ran executes nothing,\n   531\t   so nothing is indexed.  A gap still marks the indexer lost.\"\n   532\t  [indexer]\n   533\t  (consume indexer (fn [ix _packet] ix)))\n   534\t\n   535\t\n   536\t(defn status\n   537\t  \"The indexer's state as the shell reports it.  It depends on the programs\n   538\t   evaluated, never on which evaluator ran them or on the shell's token,\n   539\t   so every VM reports the same status for the same inputs.\"\n   540\t  [indexer]\n   541\t  {:transactions (:transactions indexer)\n   542\t   :published? (and (some? (:manifest-address indexer))\n   543\t                    (= (:published indexer) (:transactions indexer)))\n   544\t   :lost? (:lost? indexer)\n   545\t   :gaps (:ingress-gaps (:observer indexer) 0)\n   546\t   :failure (:failure indexer)})\n   547\t\n   548\t\n   549\t(defn notice\n   550\t  \"What the round from `before` to `after` must tell the user, or nil: a\n   551\t   lost indexer (the round's code was not indexed), or a new failure (the\n   552\t   round's code was not committed or its publication is not readable).\n   553\t   A failure's `:stage` is `:project`, `:transact`, `:materialize` or\n   554\t   `:publish`.\"\n   555\t  [before after]\n   556\t  (let [{:keys [stage outcome message]} (:failure after)]\n   557\t    (cond\n   558\t      (:lost? after)\n   559\t      (str \"Warning: the code index lost a program batch; this round's code\"\n   560\t           \" was not indexed, and indexing is suspended until (reset)\")\n   561\t\n   562\t      (and (= :materialize (:stage (:failure before))) (nil? (:failure after)))\n   563\t      (str \"Note: the code index caught up: rows of earlier rounds are now\"\n   564\t           \" written, and this round is published\")\n   565\t\n   566\t      (not= (:failure before) (:failure after))\n   567\t      (str \"Warning: this round's code is not in the published code index (\"\n   568\t           (name stage) \" failed\"\n   569\t           (when-let [detail (or message (some-> outcome name))]\n   570\t             (str \": \" detail))\n   571\t           \")\"))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
