est-address manifest))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:238:                                :published-payloads :manifest-address\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:363:  (let [{:keys [cursor transactions manifest-address manifest max-t]}\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:365:    (when (and manifest-address\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:366:               (= manifest-address (:manifest-address ix))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:371:        (let [candidate {:manifest-address manifest-address\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:410:        {:cursor cursor :manifest manifest :manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest)})\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:431:          {:keys [manifest-address manifest cursor]} (enqueue-publication ix)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:435:        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:437:              (write-head! manifest-address))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:439:                           :manifest-address manifest-address\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:444:                                             :manifest-address manifest-address\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:542:   :published? (and (some? (:manifest-address indexer))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc:429:                                           (:manifest-address indexer)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc:760:   it linked through the linker, `{name manifest-address}` -- a linked\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:351:           :head-fn (fn [manifest-address]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:352:                      ((:head-fn base) manifest-address)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:353:                      (dht/announce! node manifest-address)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:354:                      (when pub (deposit-head! pub manifest-address)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:879:  \"`{name manifest-address}` of the modules a VM module `registry` holds\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:2471:   opts: :budget; :yin.k/admitted-modules, a composition-supplied {name manifest-address}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1278:(defn- manifest-address\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1379:        address (manifest-address response)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:271:     :yin.k/admitted-modules  optional {name manifest-address} supplied\ntest/resources/yin/repl/transcripts/local.edn:18:       \"(repl-state)\"]\n## Reproduction (deliverable 2): executed on shiva, failure captured\n\nThe sandbox `ssh` binary dies on `getpwuid` (uid 501) and raw sockets are proxy-only; resolved by tunnelling SSH through the sandbox HTTP proxy (CONNECT to `shiva.stigmergy.systems:22`, host key verified against `known_hosts`, key auth as `sto`). Clone verified: `nightly-reds-fix @ 4f772d61`. Exact remote command executed:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/ci/datomworld-nightly-node\neval \"$(~/.local/bin/mise env -s bash)\"\nDATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.clojure.stream-eval-test\n```\n\nResult: `FAIL in (every-vm-answers-the-same-stream-script) (yang/clojure/stream_eval_test.cljc:444:23)` — \"repl-state agrees up to the VM's name and the medium's identity\"; `Ran 13 tests containing 309 assertions. 1 failures, 0 errors.` All four summaries share `:transactions 15`, `:rows 75`, `:occurrences 117`, cursor position 15, and differ only in `:index-publication :manifest-address` (in `vm-types` order):\n\n| VM | manifest-address |\n|---|---|\n| `:ast-walker` | `:segment/blake3-7f4fa4f0abfdba190e898342ee2a34406ee0581bf68096f65765b1c547b14afd` |\n| `:semantic` | `:segment/blake3-e9ab9489128f759d88706062efcf82307837806d5d89754873d20f81bf5042a3` |\n| `:stack` | `:segment/blake3-94191002ca99ca4459de8660220af7868a59342486911f6b65d6b8754df708c0` |\n| `:register` | `:segment/blake3-b94d127e8fa5a1058d60fa04beb4a06c1df4a8ecf26c62502fa90d2df4363f42` |\n\nNo scratch edits were made anywhere; post-run `git status` on the clone shows only the pre-existing untracked `.flutter-plugins-dependencies`. No other suites were run.\n\n## Proposed minimal fix (deliverable 3): stop publishing the provenance-bearing address in the serializable summary\n\nIn [repl.cljc:2209](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2209), drop `:manifest-address` from `:index-publication` (keep `:cursor :transactions`); update the pinning assertion at [index_test.cljc:288](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:288). The manifest address correctly hashes provenance-bearing content — changing indexed datoms would break provenance queries, recovery, and HEAD/DHT semantics, which read the indexer directly. The token-independence contract already exists for reporting ([status](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:536): \"never on … the shell's token\"); the summary should honor it, as the test already treats seals and medium identities as differing by design. Coverage is still cross-checked via cursor plus transaction count.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
